---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	title: "Cluster Admin",
	description: "Internal reference for Markovich Lab HPC cluster administration.",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-semibold">Cluster Admin</h2>
	<p class="text-muted mb-8 text-sm">Internal reference — not linked from nav. Share this URL with a Claude session to provide cluster context.</p>

	<!-- HARDWARE -->
	<section class="mb-10">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">Hardware</h3>
		<div class="overflow-x-auto">
			<table class="w-full text-sm">
				<thead><tr class="border-b text-left">
					<th class="pb-2 pr-6">Host</th><th class="pb-2 pr-6">Role</th><th class="pb-2 pr-6">Specs</th><th class="pb-2">IP</th>
				</tr></thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y">
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">headnode</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">CM + Submit</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Mac mini, Apple Silicon</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">192.168.1.10</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">worker01</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Execute</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Mac mini, 48 GB, 1 TB</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">192.168.1.21</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">worker02</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Execute</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Mac mini, 48 GB, 1 TB</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">192.168.1.12</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">worker03–06</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Execute</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Mac mini, 48 GB, 1 TB</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">192.168.1.13–16</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">nas</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">NFS storage</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Synology RS1221+</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">192.168.1.50</td></tr>
					<tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono">switch</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Network</td><td class="py-2 pr-6">Dell N4032, MTU 9216</td><td class="py-2 font-mono">10.0.0.2 (OOB)</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="text-muted mt-3 text-sm">
			<strong>Tailscale:</strong> headnode at <code>100.115.148.79</code>, advertises route <code>192.168.1.0/24</code>.<br />
			<strong>NAS mount:</strong> <code>192.168.1.50:/volume1/labdata → /Volumes/labdata</code> (NFS, resvport, MTU 9000). /etc/fstab entry on each node: <code>192.168.1.50:/volume1/labdata /Volumes/labdata nfs resvport 0 0</code>
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- HTCONDOR -->
	<section class="mb-10">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">HTCondor</h3>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm">Native ARM64 build from source. Pool password + token auth (<code>use security:recommended</code>). Execute dir: <code>/usr/local/condor/execute.noindex</code> (<code>.noindex</code> prevents Spotlight indexing). LaunchDaemon at <code>/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.htcondor.condor.plist</code> with <code>KeepAlive: true</code> (NOT NetworkState — that prevents startup at boot).</p>

		<h4 class="mb-1 font-semibold">Head node config <span class="text-muted font-normal">(/usr/local/condor/local/config.d/01-headnode.config)</span></h4>
		<pre class="bg-card mb-4 overflow-x-auto rounded p-4 text-xs"><code>CONDOR_HOST = 192.168.1.10
NETWORK_INTERFACE = 192.168.1.10
DEFAULT_DOMAIN_NAME = local
use role : get_htcondor_central_manager
use role : get_htcondor_submit
FILE_TRANSFER_DISK_LOAD_THROTTLE = 10000
FILE_TRANSFER_NETWORK_LOAD_THROTTLE = 10000
MAX_CONCURRENT_UPLOADS = 100
MAX_CONCURRENT_DOWNLOADS = 100</code></pre>

		<h4 class="mb-1 font-semibold">Worker config <span class="text-muted font-normal">(/usr/local/condor/local/config.d/01-worker.config)</span></h4>
		<pre class="bg-card mb-4 overflow-x-auto rounded p-4 text-xs"><code>CONDOR_HOST = 192.168.1.10
NETWORK_INTERFACE = 192.168.1.XX   # each worker's own IP
use role : get_htcondor_execute
EXECUTE = /usr/local/condor/execute.noindex</code></pre>

		<h4 class="mb-1 font-semibold">Quick commands</h4>
		<pre class="bg-card overflow-x-auto rounded p-4 text-xs"><code># Status / queue
condor_status
condor_q

# Logs (headnode)
tail -f /usr/local/condor/local/log/ShadowLog   # file transfer, SECMAN errors
tail -f /usr/local/condor/local/log/SchedLog    # negotiation

# Restart HTCondor
sudo launchctl stop com.htcondor.condor && sudo launchctl start com.htcondor.condor

# Clean stale execute dirs (if DiskUsage scans are slow)
sudo rm -rf /usr/local/condor/execute.noindex/dir_*</code></pre>
	</section>

	<!-- WORKFLOW -->
	<section class="mb-10">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">PEST++/PANTHER Workflow</h3>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm">
			<code>pestpp-ies</code> runs as master on headnode; 84 HTCondor jobs act as PANTHER workers over TCP.
			Project directory: <code>/Users/kmarkovich/mf_insar/</code>. Conda env: <code>mf_insar</code> (packed with conda-pack into <code>mf_insar.tar.gz</code> for file transfer).
			Environment requires <code>pandas&lt;3</code> (pyemu breaks with pandas≥3); pyemu and flopy from develop branches.
		</p>
		<p class="mb-3 text-sm">
			<strong>Critical setting in workflow.py:</strong> <code>overdue_giveup_minutes=15</code> — keep this low. A high value (e.g. 1440) causes 8-hour iteration stalls when one worker hangs.
			Kill requests in the <code>.rmr</code> file are normal — PANTHER kills duplicate runs when one agent already returned a result.
		</p>
		<p class="text-sm">
			<strong>Memory:</strong> <code>request_memory = 3072</code> in submit file; actual RSS per worker process is ~150–186 MB (verified via <code>ps aux</code>). Reservation is fine, headroom is ample (48 GB / 14 cores).
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- KNOWN ISSUES -->
	<section class="mb-10">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">Known Issues</h3>
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">

			<div class="bg-card rounded-lg p-4">
				<h4 class="font-semibold">1. Worker first-activation failure (SECMAN:2007)</h4>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">First slot activation attempt fails, second succeeds. Root cause: macOS TCC local network permission on unsigned binaries. <strong>Not fully resolved — accepted as known behavior.</strong> Mitigation: keep <code>overdue_giveup_minutes=15</code> so stalled first attempts reschedule fast.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="bg-card rounded-lg p-4">
				<h4 class="font-semibold">2. eduroam WiFi / Tailscale outage</h4>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">Headnode is on eduroam WiFi. Periodic certificate expiry silently drops internet without disconnecting from the SSID — Tailscale goes offline. Fix: physically visit headnode, open a browser, re-accept eduroam cert. <strong>Long-term fix: request a wired university jack from UNM IT.</strong> When re-running <code>tailscale up</code>, must include <code>--accept-dns=false</code>.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="bg-card rounded-lg p-4">
				<h4 class="font-semibold">3. Stale execute directory accumulation</h4>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">If HTCondor is killed mid-job, per-job <code>dir_*</code> subdirectories under <code>/usr/local/condor/execute.noindex/</code> are never cleaned up. With 100k+ dirs, DiskUsage scans take 136–166 seconds per job start. Fix: <code>sudo rm -rf /usr/local/condor/execute.noindex/dir_*</code>. <code>condor_preen</code> runs daily at 8:31am to prevent re-accumulation.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="bg-card rounded-lg p-4">
				<h4 class="font-semibold">4. DNS PTR record on worker01 (resolved)</h4>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">worker01's old IP <code>192.168.1.11</code> had a UNM reverse DNS record (<code>osa-camp-dt-7.colleges.ad.unm.edu</code>) causing HTCondor connection delays and 8-hour iteration stalls. Fixed by changing worker01 IP to <code>192.168.1.21</code> (returns NXDOMAIN). Verify with <code>host 192.168.1.21</code> — should show NXDOMAIN. If adding future workers, verify their IPs have no PTR record before using them.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="bg-card rounded-lg p-4">
				<h4 class="font-semibold">5. Miniforge must be installed as user, not root</h4>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">Install to <code>~/miniforge3</code> without sudo. Installing to <code>/opt/miniforge3</code> as root causes permission errors on every conda operation. If this happened: <code>sudo rm -rf /opt/miniforge3</code>, then reinstall as user.</p>
			</div>

		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- SOFTWARE -->
	<section class="mb-10">
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">Software &amp; Remote Access</h3>
		<ul class="text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
			<li>Homebrew → Node.js → Claude Code (<code>npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code</code>)</li>
			<li>Miniforge at <code>~/miniforge3</code> (per-user, no sudo)</li>
			<li>conda-pack for bundling <code>mf_insar</code> env for HTCondor</li>
			<li>Tailscale (<code>brew install tailscale</code>); always use <code>--accept-dns=false</code></li>
			<li>Amphetamine (App Store) for lid-closed operation on MacBook Air (M4, 24 GB, 512 GB)</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<!-- PENDING -->
	<section>
		<h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold">Pending / To-Do</h3>
		<ul class="text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
			<li>Set <code>overdue_giveup_minutes=15</code> in <code>deploy_pestpp()</code> in <code>/Users/kmarkovich/mf_insar/workflow.py</code></li>
			<li>Request wired university Ethernet jack from UNM IT for server room</li>
			<li>Set up DSM email alerts on Synology NAS for drive failure</li>
			<li>Add cluster-docs repo link here once repo is public</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
